<!--
    regnarrow controls on x86-64 (clang -Os and gcc -O2 of generated functions).
        f0000 at 0x40203d: a 32-bit value kept zero-extended in r12 is passed to
               `sinkl(long)` (`mov edi,r12d; call sinkl`) and also read as
               `(long)(int)v >> 3`.  Narrowing its web to four bytes handed the
               call the 32-bit value, and the signed read declared it `int`, so
               the C sign-extended the argument where the binary zero-extends
               it.  A web of `int` width read by a wider parameter is left at the
               register's width (#1, #2).
        f0017 at 0x403080: a product's high half lives in the upper half of
               rcx, a register piece no register name covers.  Once the narrowed
               byte web no longer merged it with esi, it printed as an undeclared
               `dat_c`; it is a local (`// register 0xc`) like any other register
               value (#3, #4).

    Stage: P3 simplification quiescence (regnarrow) and P6 variable naming.
    P0 assertion: option regnarrow on|off.  Pass 1 (default on) proves the
    fixes; pass 2 (off) is the register-wide baseline f0000 always had (#1).
-->
